/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * assets/i18n-uk.js — the localisation layer. Loaded BEFORE assets/pipeline.js;
 * the renderer reads what this file declares, so the order in index.html
 * matters and must not be swapped.
 *
 * Holds: the I18N and RT declarations, the runtime strings in both locales, the
 * Ukrainian artifact labels (ART_UK), the step-to-artifact map (APPEARS_AT) and
 * the three Ukrainian dictionary slices (UK-SLICES / UK-CRITERIA / UK-PROMPTS).
 *
 * Humans and agents may edit this file when wording changes; it carries no
 * project state. The state contract lives in index.html, in
 * <script type="application/json" id="pipeline-data"> — nothing here.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* ===========================================================================
 * Localisation dictionary.
 *
 * I18N.en is NOT hand-written: it is captured from the markup on load, so the
 * English the page ships with (and shows with JavaScript disabled) can never
 * drift from the English in this dictionary. Every translatable element in the
 * markup carries data-i18n="<key>"; that key is the dictionary key.
 *
 * I18N.uk is the explicit translation, keyed by the same ids. Prompt blocks
 * (<pre class="prompt-body">) and /dsf:* command names are deliberately NOT
 * translated — they are pasted into the agent chat verbatim in both locales.
 *
 * This lives outside the pipeline-data JSON block on purpose: agents replace
 * only that JSON, and must never touch this.
 * ======================================================================== */
